  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, PCA, ResNet50, concat) outperformed config_001 (RNA-only PCA) by ~4.2% accuracy, confirming that adding an image branch with concat fusion is beneficial. Uncertainty: We have no evidence yet on whether multiprofile (aggregating multiple cell profiles per sample) improves over singleprofile in the multimodal setting. This is a fundamental architectural decision that, if positive, would unlock a large subset of configurations and potentially yield further gains. config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, PCA, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) is the most direct logical extension of the best-performing config_016, changing only the profile setting (single→multi) and adding the corresponding avgpool aggregation while keeping fusion=concat fixed. This isolates the multiprofile/aggregation question as the primary new variable. Under a limited budget, resolving whether multiprofile helps is more informative than testing minor fusion variants (e.g., weighted vs concat) because it determines whether an entire axis of the search space is worth further exploration."
}

